{
  "$comment": "SecurityInsight relations BETWEEN CIs -- the asset graph (template kind: relation). Each item turns one SI field of a CI into typed, directional relations: from (this CI) -> to. target: 'ci' = the field holds CI ids; 'id' = the field holds an identifier of type idType -- the relation points at the CI that carries that identifier, or at the identifier itself when no CI does; 'node' = the field names something that is not a CI (a subscription, a group, a role) of type nodeType. reverse: the relation runs from the field's CI to this CI (a user signs in to this device). valuePath: for a list of objects, the properties to read the value from, first non-empty wins; detailPath: the same for the relation's detail (a role name). stage: production relations are written; testing and not_used ones are not. Customer overrides: relations.custom.json (Community) or an item override in Template conformance (Pro), per relation id.",
  "kind": "relation",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "relations": [
    {
      "id": "owned_by",
